  "id": "fdaee3b2-cdcb-49c7-9342-0d26b56539ad",
  "title": "SC seeks Centre's response on social media risks to children",
  "summary": "The Supreme Court sought the Centre and the National Commission for Protection of Child Rights (NCPCR) to respond to a PIL filed by an Indore-based school, requesting a national framework to protect children from online risks like grooming, cyberbullying, and harmful content.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "The Supreme Court sought the Centre's response to a plea for age-based social media restrictions and safeguards to protect children from online exploitation and harmful content.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The court ordered the ministries of women and child development and law and justice, and the NCPCR, to issue notices to address the school's concerns.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The court also tagged the plea, filed by Emerald Heights International School, pending its hearing on December 7.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
